    "estimated_hours": 3.0,
    "goal": "Plan scoring-should-stop-a-promotion §3: the reflex fires on the path a healthy run takes. Two of the section's own tests are red on main:\n- tests/test_review_reflex_sweep.py::test_a_refused_review_leaves_the_rest_of_the_wave_dispatched\n- ::test_a_recorded_refusal_is_the_report_and_not_a_generator\n\nBoth fail with IndexError at :331 (report[\"reviews\"][\"refused\"][0]). The fixture produced its refusal from a member-seat collision. ecd1528c removed that collision by design, when every unnamed dispatch got a disposable member. So the refusal-continuation property is no longer exercised.\n\nMake a per-run review refusal reachable again in the sweep fixture, through a path that still refuses: a scope conflict, a budget refusal or a lane refusal. Keep the assertions that the refused run is recorded as the report and that the other runs in the wave were still dispatched. Change reckon/crew/recovery.py only if dispatch_awaiting_reviews itself mishandles the refusal. Confirm first that both tests still fail at the dispatch base.",
